  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nHigh pressure to the south of the region will keep moisture \naway from the area as a weak cold front enters and washes out \noverhead. Weather will remain dry despite the front in the \nregion with 40s dew points in place. High temperatures today \nwill be in the 70s but will cool off a bit on Tuesday behind the\nfront, especially areas closest to Lake Erie. High pressure \nreturns from the north for Tuesday and Wednesday, retaining dry\nweather across the region. This system will push east of the\narea by Thursday, allowing a warm front through the area. High\ntemperatures on Thursday will be the warmest for the week, up \nto the mid 70s in some spots. A cold front will approach on\nThursday night and may bring some rain to NE OH/NW PA, but the\nbest upper level support may be northeast of the area. High\npressure will return for Friday and Saturday with more dry\nweather and 60s/70s. The next rain system will approach on\nSaturday night and may be more of a story for Sunday.",
